CI run #15 (first full-gate run of this branch on GitHub) exposed that
9-10 tests pass locally but fail under the runner's environment, plus
a latent pip-audit defect. All reproduced locally under the exact CI
environment and fixed:

* Rich/typer styles CLI panels even without a TTY when GITHUB_ACTIONS
  is set, so option spellings like --version/--authorization/--result
  are emitted with ANSI escapes inside them. Four CLI-contract tests
  now normalize ANSI before asserting (rt_v88 _err_text, hunt
  authorization refusal, r4 help contract, umdr30 flag contract) —
  the contract under test is the text, not the styling.
* Four tests asserted defaults or designed paths that the CI
  production contract (LLM_ENABLED=false, DISABLE_RAG=true,
  EMBEDDINGS_OFFLINE=true) overrides. They now isolate their
  environment explicitly (delenv + get_settings.cache_clear), and the
  crawler structure-aware override test patches the module-level
  is_llm_enabled binding its subject actually consults:
  v10 embeddings defaults, refutation planner advisory, v28 llm-bias
  override, v62 lesson scope contract.
* ci.yml SBOM step: uv export lacked --no-emit-project, so the
  requirements file carried the editable project itself and pip-audit
  cannot install/hash it under --require-hashes (internal pip failure,
  silently swallowed by || true). With --no-emit-project the audit
  resolves against real artifacts only (same flag the VIP gate's
  export already uses).

Static gates re-verified on the fixed tree: ruff ratchet 8005<8147,
markers, deps-gate, secrets, bandit, coverage ratchet, test-count
floor — all green.
